# undertown: what lies under the town the company begins in, a step from its door (the owner, 1 November 2026: "we shouldn't have to explore to start an adventuring loop").
// A Kyr template (see src/world/kyr-template.ts). {t} is the town's id, {town} its name; "{{t}_merchant}" is
// written "{s2_merchant}", the merchant's name when it is read. The base and below are always written; of each other
// group one option is drawn for the town. An option of the store, the yard or the pit is a trouble: its name is the
// {pack} and {pair} are how many of the small and middling foes a trouble sets (three and two for one, five and three for
// a company); {brood} is how many of the first foes each trouble sets: two for a company of more than one, one for a company of
// one, as a player begins (a lone first-level mage had died to the corn-store's two great rats three times in four).
// id of the foe it sets there ({t}_u_<option>) and of the job of being rid of it ({t}_u_<option>_job), and its ">>"
// lines are what is said of it on the notice on the green. Add an option to add a trouble; nothing in the engine
// needs to change.
--- base
  // Each fight under the town is worth three times its plain worth, so that a company that clears all of it (some
  // thousand) comes to the stair below the vault at the second level, not the first (the builder's descent of 8
  // November: a lone warrior cleared the town's ten fights at level one, and died at the first of the deep site).
  Relation {t}_u_paid(entity). Relation {t}_u_done(entity). Relation {t}_u_given(entity).
  // A job half paid for (done, its cause not yet seen to) is paid only the rest when it is finished (REV-21: the
  // half and then the whole had both been paid).
  Relation {t}_u_halved(entity).
  // A job paid is no longer a lead: its knowing is let go, and it is told among what is done (the Book had listed
  // finished jobs under "Leads: heard, not yet seen": M19-121).
  Place {t}_u_store "the old corn-store" is room within {t} at 0, 1 indoors.
  // Each way down is locked or barred by whoever is troubled by what is under it, and given by them with the job: the
  // troubles had been done without a word to anyone, and paid for after (the owner, 3 November).
  Kind corn_store_key "the corn-store key" like cell_key described "A heavy iron key on a loop of string, with the corn-store's mark burned into its wooden tag.".
  Kind crypt_key "the crypt key" like cell_key described "A long black key, worn smooth, for the stone door into the catacombs under the churchyard.".
  Kind quarry_key "the key to the quarry gate" like cell_key described "A small brass padlock key, for the gate the inn put across the old quarry's adit.".
  Passage {t}_u_store_door "the corn-store door" is door between {t}_green and {t}_u_store.
  // Each locked way is a lock on it: whoever the job is given to holds its key and goes through as if it were open,
  // and anyone with lockwork can pick it instead (Mission 19, a calling's own way in: a thief need not ask).
  Thing {t}_u_store_lock "the corn-store padlock" on {t}_u_store_door {
    // Locked, the padlock is said when the door is tried or the padlock looked at, not as part of the green.
    State locked blocking "".
    State open "The corn-store padlock hangs open on its hasp.".
    Change pick "Pick the corn-store padlock" from locked to open needing lockwork.
    Change wrench "Wrench the padlock's hasp out of the old door" from locked to torn needing brawn.
    State torn "The hasp hangs out of the corn-store door by one bolt, the oak split round it.".
  }
  // Torn out, it is noticed by whoever owns the store, once, when the company is next before them: a cold player tore
  // the hasp out without asking for the key, and was paid for the rats as if nothing had been done (Mission 20, D).
  Relation {t}_u_hasp_noted(entity).
  Rule {t}_u_hasp_seen when state({t}_u_store_lock, torn) and together({t}_merchant, party) and not {t}_u_hasp_noted({t}_u_store_lock) says "{{t}_merchant} does not look up. 'Somebody tore the hasp out of my corn-store door. I had a key for whoever asked.' A look at your hands, then. 'I'll know them by the splinters.'" { Assert {t}_u_hasp_noted({t}_u_store_lock). }
  Observe {t}_u_store_lock_shut near {t}_u_store_lock of {t}_u_store_lock when state({t}_u_store_lock, locked) "A padlock the size of a fist hangs on the corn-store door, its hasp bolted through the old oak.".
  Place {t}_u_yard "the churchyard" is room within {t} at 1, 2 outdoors.
  Passage {t}_u_yard_gate "the lych-gate" is gate between {t}_green and {t}_u_yard.
  Place {t}_u_pit "the old quarry pit" is room within {t} at 2, 2 outdoors.
  Passage {t}_u_pit_path "the path down into the old quarry" is path between {t}_green and {t}_u_pit taking 5 minutes.
  Place {t}_u_cellar "the corn-store cellar" is room within {t} at 0, 3 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_trap "the trapdoor" is stair between {t}_u_store and {t}_u_cellar.
  Place {t}_u_warren "the rat-runs" is room within {t} at 0, 4 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_runs "a hole gnawed through the cellar wall" is crawl between {t}_u_cellar and {t}_u_warren.
  Place {t}_u_nest "the nest" is room within {t} at 0, 6 underground 2 down.
  Passage {t}_u_nest_way "the rats' run down" is crawl between {t}_u_warren and {t}_u_nest.
  Passage {t}_u_nest_shelf "a shelf above the water" is passage between {t}_u_nest and {t}_u_drain.
  Place {t}_u_crypt "the crypt" is room within {t} at 1, 3 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_crypt_stair "the stone stair under the churchyard" is stair between {t}_u_yard and {t}_u_crypt.
  Thing {t}_u_crypt_lock "the lock of the stone door" on {t}_u_crypt_stair {
    // Locked, said when the door is tried or the lock looked at, as the corn-store's padlock is: told in the room,
    // it said the crypt's door was locked to a company come through it with the key (round 9, Q 74).
    State locked blocking "".
    State open "The stone door into the ground stands unlocked.".
    Change pick "Pick the old lock of the stone door" from locked to open needing lockwork.
    // And forced, as any door may be by one strong enough (the owner's evidence session, 7 November: a warrior of
    // twenty strength stood at this door with nothing to do but go and ask for the key).
    Change force "Set your shoulder to the stone door until the old lock gives" from locked to open needing brawn.
  }
  Place {t}_u_ossuary "the ossuary" is room within {t} at 1, 4 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_bone_arch "an arch stacked round with skulls" is arch between {t}_u_crypt and {t}_u_ossuary.
  Place {t}_u_adit "the quarry adit" is room within {t} at 2, 3 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_adit_mouth "the gated adit" is passage between {t}_u_pit and {t}_u_adit.
  Thing {t}_u_adit_lock "the padlock on the adit gate" on {t}_u_adit_mouth {
    State locked blocking "".
    State open "The adit gate's padlock hangs open on its chain.".
    Change pick "Pick the brass padlock" from locked to open needing lockwork.
    Change force "Wrench the adit gate's padlock off its staple" from locked to open needing brawn.
  }
  Place {t}_u_gallery "the cut gallery" is room within {t} at 2, 4 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_gallery_way "the old cutting" is passage between {t}_u_adit and {t}_u_gallery.
  // Behind the gallery, where the boy saw the big one: the spiders' mother and her eggs.
  Place {t}_u_brood "the brood-chamber" is room within {t} at 3, 4 underground 1 down.
  Passage {t}_u_brood_way "a crack at the back of the gallery, hung with web" is crawl between {t}_u_gallery and {t}_u_brood.
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_cellar). Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_warren). Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_crypt).
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_ossuary). Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_adit). Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_gallery).
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_nest).
  // The corn-store, locked behind the company, is somewhere to rest between the brood and the nest.
  Initially Assert restful({t}_u_store).
  // What each room under the town is, said on coming down into it (the cellar had said nothing at all: a play of a1's
  // rats on 3 November).
  Observe {t}_u_cellar_scene at {t}_u_cellar as fixture when true "A low brick cellar under the corn-store, damp to the touch, with spilled grain trodden black on the floor and the droppings of something bigger than mice.".
  Observe {t}_u_warren_scene at {t}_u_warren as fixture when true "A crawlway of earth and old brick behind the cellar wall, gnawed wider than any rat should need, littered with husks, bones and the stink of a nest.".
  Observe {t}_u_crypt_scene at {t}_u_crypt as fixture when true "A vaulted crypt under the churchyard, its shelves of coffins pushed askew; the dust on the floor is scuffed through in a dozen places by feet that dragged.".
  Observe {t}_u_ossuary_scene at {t}_u_ossuary as fixture when true "Bones stacked to the roof in patient courses, skulls set in rows along the top like a frieze, and gaps in the courses where some have lately been taken down.".
  Observe {t}_u_adit_scene at {t}_u_adit as fixture when true "The old quarry's adit runs straight into the hill, its walls marked with the bite of picks, and grey threads of web across it at the height of a face.".
  Observe {t}_u_gallery_scene at {t}_u_gallery as fixture when true "A gallery cut square out of the rock, wider than it is high, where the stone was taken out in blocks; the roof here is thick with web, and the web is thick with husks.".
--- store rats
  // The rats: the corn-store is locked and its key is the merchant's, given with the job. A brood in the runs behind
  // the cellar wall, and below them, down their own run into the old drain, the nest and the old buck rat that keeps
  // it: a job of two fights, or of ratsbane and fire for a company that would rather not (Mission 19: the owner found
  // two rats and "it is done" too short to be worth it). The drain below the runs is the undertown's road (see
  // the section below).
  Observe {t}_u_store_scene at {t}_u_store as fixture when true "Sacks stacked to the rafters, and the smell of mice; a trapdoor in the floor with a sack of grain weighting it down, and gnawed holes along the foot of every wall.".
  Person {t}_u_rats "the rats under the corn-store" at {t}_u_warren {
    Role "rats, fat and bold, that have eaten their way into the corn-store from below". Species rat.{runts} Numbers {pack}. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_warren.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_rats) to 60.
  Person {t}_u_buck "the old buck rat" at {t}_u_nest {
    Role "a rat the size of a dog, grey at the muzzle, with a torn ear and the run of the drain". Species great_rat. Variant elder. Numbers 1. Level 2. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_nest.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_buck) to 120.
  Entity {t}_u_rats_job: fact "Clear the rats out of the corn-store cellar, under the old corn-store at {town}.".
  Entity {t}_u_rats_source: fact "The rats come up into the cellar by a run of their own from their nest below, over the old drain.".
  Topic {t}_u_rats_job_ask with {t}_merchant "Ask {{t}_merchant} about the rats in the corn-store" when not {t}_u_given({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) once {
    Says "'They've got into the old corn-store from underneath,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'Rats, a whole nest of them, and bold with it. I've lost a third of the grain.' A key comes off a nail behind the counter. 'There's a trapdoor in the floor. Kill them, and find where they're getting in, or they'll be back by harvest. Ten coin, and I'll see you right for a lantern besides.' And, looking you over: 'Or lay ratsbane where they come up, if you'd sooner not be bitten. It wants a night.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_rats_job). Assert {t}_u_given({t}_u_rats_job). Give corn_store_key to actor. Assert keyholder(actor, {t}_u_store_lock). }
  }
  Observe {t}_u_rats_run_seen at {t}_u_warren as sign when not knows(party, {t}_u_rats_source) "Along the back wall of the runs the rats have worn a path in the dirt, and it goes down through the old brickwork, toward the smell of the drain." teaches {t}_u_rats_source.
  Observe {t}_u_nest_scene at {t}_u_nest as fixture when true "A dry shelf above the drain water, heaped with chewed sacking, straw and grain-husks, and bones under it all; the stink is enough to make the eyes run.".
  // Nothing done to the nest from far off: the buck rat is too old for bait, but not for fire.
  Action {t}_u_nest_burned(actor: group, site: place) "Throw an oil firebomb into the nest" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and (at(actor, {t}_u_warren) or at(actor, {t}_u_drain)) and holding(actor, oil_firebomb) and able({t}_u_buck).
    Time 1 minutes.
    On success { Spend oil_firebomb from actor. Slay {t}_u_buck. }
    Result "The flask bursts on the shelf and the straw goes up at once. Something big comes out of it screaming and goes into the water, and does not come up again.".
  }
  // A magician's way with the rats themselves: a sleep laid over the run, and the rats done for where they lie
  // (Mission 19's Priority Three), for one who would not be bitten. A mage's charm, not the Sleep spell, which a mage
  // need not have (round 5's evoker was offered "a spell of sleep" she had never learned).
  Action {t}_u_rats_slept(actor: group, site: place) "Put the rats in the run to sleep with a mage's charm, and do for them where they lie" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_warren) and able({t}_u_rats) and memberOf(?m, actor) and awake(?m) and (hasCalling(?m, calling_mage) or learned(?m, sleep)).
    Time 1 minutes.
    On success { Slay {t}_u_rats. }
    Result "The words go out over the run like a breath of cold air, and the rats slow, and stagger, and lie down where they were. It is quick, after that, and not pleasant, and none of them wakes for it.".
  }
  Rule {t}_u_rats_cleared when not able({t}_u_rats) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job). }
  Relation {t}_u_nest_cleared(entity).
  Rule {t}_u_nest_ended when not able({t}_u_buck) and not {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) { Assert {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job). }
  Discovery {t}_u_nest_hoard "Under the nest's sacking, what the rats dragged in over the years." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_nest "Under the chewed sacking something catches the light.".
  }
  Item {t}_u_nest_ring "a cord of grave rings" is grave_rings at {t}_u_nest hidden until {t}_u_nest_hoard.
  // A way through that needs no fight for the brood in the runs (a lone mage or thief had no way through the first
  // jobs): ratsbane from the chandler's, laid where the rats come up into the cellar, does its work by morning.
  Relation {t}_u_baited(group). Measure {t}_u_baited_at(group).
  Action {t}_u_rats_baited(actor: group, site: place) "Lay ratsbane where the rats come up into the cellar" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_cellar) and holding(actor, ratsbane) and able({t}_u_rats) and not {t}_u_baited({t}_u_rats).
    Time 1.
    On success { Spend ratsbane from actor. Assert {t}_u_baited({t}_u_rats). Set {t}_u_baited_at({t}_u_rats) to watch(clock). }
    Result "You lay the ratsbane in twists along the foot of the wall where the droppings are thickest. Something scrabbles behind the brick, and goes quiet. By morning, it will have done its work.".
  }
  Rule {t}_u_rats_poisoned when {t}_u_baited({t}_u_rats) and able({t}_u_rats) and watch(clock) >= {t}_u_baited_at({t}_u_rats) + 36 { Slay {t}_u_rats. }
  Objective {t}_u_rats_job_sought when knows(party, {t}_u_notice) and not {t}_u_given({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) toward {t}_merchant "Ask {{t}_merchant} about the rats in the corn-store at {town}: the corn-store is locked.".
  Objective {t}_u_rats_job_aim when {t}_u_given({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) toward {t}_u_cellar by {t}_u_store "Clear the rats out of {{t}_u_cellar}, under {{t}_u_store} at {town}, and find where they get in.".
  Objective {t}_u_rats_job_run when {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and knows(party, {t}_u_rats_source) and not {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) toward {t}_u_nest, {t}_u_buck by {t}_u_warren "Clear the rats' nest, down their run from {{t}_u_warren} under {{t}_u_store}, and the old buck rat that keeps it, or they will be back.".
  Topic {t}_u_rats_job_paid with {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} the rats under the corn-store are dead, nest and all" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_halved({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_merchant} hears about the drain and the old buck rat with a face that says the grain is the least of it. Ten coin are counted out, and a lantern and two flasks of oil set on the counter beside them. 'That drain goes under half the town,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'If you're going back down it, go with a light that won't blow out.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Give lantern to actor. Give 2 lamp_oil to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_rats_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_rats_job_rest with {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} the rats' nest in the drain is cleared" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_halved({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_merchant} hears about the drain and the old buck rat, and counts out the other four coin, and sets a lantern and two flasks of oil on the counter beside them. 'That drain goes under half the town,' says {{t}_merchant}. 'If you're going back down it, go with a light that won't blow out.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 4. Give lantern to actor. Give 2 lamp_oil to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_rats_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_rats_job_half with {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} the rats under the corn-store are dead" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) once {
    Says "'Dead,' says {{t}_merchant}, 'and the rest of them coming up the same way they came, I don't doubt.' Six coin are counted out. 'Find where they come from and clear it, and you'll have the other four, and the lantern.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 6. Assert {t}_u_halved({t}_u_rats_job). }
  }
  // Owed only to a company that took the job, and "the rest" only once half was paid: one that had killed the rats
  // unasked had been told of the rest of a pay it had never been offered (round 6, I 144, J 38).
  Objective {t}_u_rats_job_owed when {t}_u_given({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_halved({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) toward {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} the rats and their nest are dealt with, at {{merchantat}}: the rest of the pay, and a lantern.".
  Objective {t}_u_rats_job_owed_whole when {t}_u_given({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and {t}_u_nest_cleared({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_halved({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_rats_job) toward {t}_merchant "Tell {{t}_merchant} the rats and their nest are dealt with, at {{merchantat}}: ten coin, and a lantern.".
>> 'RATS in the old corn-store, a nest of them. Ten coin, and a lantern. Ask {{t}_merchant} for the key.'
  Rule {t}_u_rats_onward when {t}_u_done({t}_u_rats_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward). }
--- yard dead
  // The dead: they have not come up of themselves. Someone has been opening graves by night and raising what was in
  // them with a black candle in the ossuary; the churchyard, the crypt and the lodger at the inn say so to whoever
  // looks, and the dead lie down again when the candle is out, by a fight or by words (the owner, 3 November: the
  // dead had come with no hint of why, and nothing to find out).
  Observe {t}_u_yard_scene at {t}_u_yard as fixture when true "Old stones leaning in the grass, and in the corner by the wall a low stone door into the ground, its iron ring bright where someone has pulled at it lately.".
  Entity {t}_u_dead_robbed: fact "Someone has been opening graves in the churchyard by night, and going down into the catacombs.".
  Entity {t}_u_dead_raised: fact "The dead under the churchyard have been raised: a ring of chalk, and the ends of black candles, are on the crypt floor.".
  Entity {t}_u_dead_lodger: fact "A man lodging at the inn goes out after dark, and comes back before light with grave-dirt on his boots.".
  Observe {t}_u_yard_graves at {t}_u_yard as sign when not knows(party, {t}_u_dead_robbed) "Three graves by the wall have been dug into and filled again badly, and the grass is trodden flat from them to the stone door." teaches {t}_u_dead_robbed.
  Observe {t}_u_crypt_circle at {t}_u_crypt as sign when not knows(party, {t}_u_dead_raised) "On the crypt floor is a ring of chalk with marks round it, and inside it the ends of black candles, burned to the floor." teaches {t}_u_dead_raised.
  Person {t}_u_dead "the hungry dead of the ossuary" at {t}_u_ossuary {
    Role "dead things raised out of the bone-heaps, hungry". Species ghoul. Numbers {brood}. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_ossuary.
  }
  Initially Assert tolerates({t}_u_dead, party).
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_dead) to 75.
  Person {t}_u_raiser "the man with the black candle" at {t}_u_ossuary {
    Role "a grave-robber who has read a book he should not have, and is trying what it says". Ancestry human. Calling mage. Level 2. Temperament defensive. Lair {t}_u_ossuary. Pronouns he.
    Warns "A man in a muddy coat stands up behind a burning black candle, among the bones. 'Go back up,' he says. 'This is not yours.'".
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_raiser) to 90.
  // His dead stand with him while the candle burns: a fight with him is with them (the man died to one blow, alone,
  // with his dead looking on: Mission 20's fourth round, F 100–101). Pinching the candle out is still the way past.
  Initially Assert beside({t}_u_dead, {t}_u_raiser).
  Thing {t}_u_candle "the black candle" at {t}_u_ossuary {
    State alight "A black candle burns on a skull in the middle of the bone-heaps, with a flame that does not move.".
    State snuffed "The black candle is out, and smells of something worse than tallow.".
    Change pinch "Pinch out the black candle" from alight to snuffed when not at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) or not able({t}_u_raiser) "The man with the black candle stands over it, and the dead are his while it burns.".
  }
  Entity {t}_u_dead_job: fact "Lay the dead in the crypt under the churchyard at {town}.".
  // Not once the job is done: a warrior who forced the crypt door and laid the dead had still been offered the job,
  // and the key, after the pay (the owner, 7 November). So for each job asked of.
  Topic {t}_u_dead_job_ask with {t}_priest "Ask {{t}_priest} about the noises under the churchyard" when not {t}_u_given({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_priest} looks at the floor. 'The catacombs. Something has come up out of the bone-heaps, and there have been lights in the churchyard at night that were not mine.' The crypt key is unhooked from a belt. 'I cannot ask anyone to go. If you will, lay them, and find out who is doing it. Fifteen coin, and what the shrine can give besides.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_job). Assert {t}_u_given({t}_u_dead_job). Give crypt_key to actor. Assert keyholder(actor, {t}_u_crypt_lock). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_dead_lodger_ask with {t}_innkeeper "Ask {{t}_innkeeper} who goes out at night" when knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_robbed) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_lodger) once {
    Says "{{t}_innkeeper} wipes the same place on the counter twice. 'There's a man in the back room, been here a fortnight, pays in old coin. Goes out after dark and comes in before light, and there's grave-dirt on his boots that I scrub off the step.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_lodger). }
  }
  // The lodger the innkeeper tells of is the man with the black candle, and is found: going down the crypt stair by
  // night, and known for himself in the ossuary (round 9, Q: told of, never found; a night watching the churchyard
  // had said "Nothing comes").
  Observe {t}_u_lodger_goes at {t}_u_yard as sign when dark() and knows(party, {t}_u_dead_lodger) and able({t}_u_raiser) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) "Late, a man in good boots crosses the churchyard with a lantern shuttered to a slit, and goes down the crypt stair without looking back. The innkeeper's lodger keeps his hours.".
  Observe {t}_u_lodger_known at {t}_u_ossuary when knows(party, {t}_u_dead_lodger) and at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) and able({t}_u_raiser) "There is grave-dirt to the ankles of his good boots: the man who lodges at the inn and pays in old coin.".
  Action {t}_u_raiser_talked(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the man with the black candle the town knows what he has done, and that it ends now" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_ossuary) and at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) and able({t}_u_raiser) and knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_raised) and state({t}_u_candle, alight).
    Time 0.
    Resolve check(actor, intimidation, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state({t}_u_candle, snuffed). Retract state({t}_u_candle, alight). Retract at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser). }
    Result "He looks at you a long time over the flame, and then at the dead. Then he wets his fingers and pinches the candle out, and goes past you up the stair without a word, and out of {town} before morning. The book he leaves on the bones.".
    Otherwise "'They'll hang me whether I stop or not,' he says, and lifts the candle higher. The dead turn their heads.".
  }
  // A priest's way, and a scholar's (Mission 19: a calling's knowledge makes a different ending): the rite of rest
  // said over the bone-heaps puts the candle out from where it stands; and one who knows the old scripts reads in the
  // chalk ring what the raiser's book left out, and can tell him so.
  Action {t}_u_dead_rested(actor: group, site: place) "Say the rite of rest over the bone-heaps, against the black candle" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_ossuary) and state({t}_u_candle, alight) and capable(actor, rites).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, rites, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state({t}_u_candle, snuffed). Retract state({t}_u_candle, alight). Retract at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser). }
    Result "You say the words for the dead that every shrine keeps, slowly, as they are meant to be said. The flame on the black candle leans as if a door had opened somewhere, and goes out. The man in the muddy coat looks at you as if you had struck him, and goes up the stair at a run, and out of {town} before morning. The book he leaves on the bones.".
    Otherwise "The words come, but the black candle's flame does not move, and the dead turn their heads toward the sound.".
  }
  // A thief's way (journey 2 of Mission 19, 7 November: the same opening played as a cleric and as a thief, the
  // cleric had the rite and a scholar the chalk, and the thief nothing of a thief's own here): round behind the
  // bone-heaps, out of his candle's light, to pinch it out from behind him. Seen, the dead are no longer his to hold.
  Action {t}_u_candle_crept(actor: group, site: place) "Creep round behind the bone-heaps and pinch out the black candle at his back" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_ossuary) and at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) and able({t}_u_raiser) and state({t}_u_candle, alight) and capable(actor, stealth).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, stealth, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert state({t}_u_candle, snuffed). Retract state({t}_u_candle, alight). Retract at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser). }
    On failure { Retract tolerates({t}_u_dead, party). }
    Result "You go back the way you came, and round, along the foot of the bone-heaps where his candle throws no light, and come up behind him. He hears nothing until the flame is a wisp between your fingers. He turns, sees the dead fall, and runs: up the stair and out of {town} before morning. The book he leaves on the bones.".
    Otherwise "A skull rolls off the course under your hand and goes down the heap, knocking. He turns with the candle held high, and the dead turn with him.".
  }
  // The book he leaves on the bones, as each ending says, is there to be taken (M19-143: it was told, and Search found
  // nothing): left when he goes, or dropped when he falls.
  Kind raiser_book "a book of the dead" is gear worth 6 weighing 1 described "A small fat book in a scraped calf binding, copied out by several hands over a long time: rites for the dead, and in the margins, in a newer hand, how they might be called back up. Someone has drawn the chalk ring on the last page and got it wrong.".
  Entity {t}_u_book_left: fact "The raiser's book of the dead lies on the bones in the ossuary.".
  Item {t}_u_raiser_book "a book of the dead" is raiser_book at {t}_u_ossuary hidden until {t}_u_book_left.
  Rule {t}_u_book_dropped when ({t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) or not able({t}_u_raiser)) and at(party, {t}_u_ossuary) and not knows(party, {t}_u_book_left) says "His book lies on the bones." teaches {t}_u_book_left { }
  Entity {t}_u_dead_read: fact "The marks round the chalk ring are copied from an old book of the dead, and copied badly: the warding line is left out. The dead are held only while the candle burns, and whoever holds them is not safe from them.".
  Observe {t}_u_crypt_marks at {t}_u_crypt as sign when capable(party, lore) and knows(party, {t}_u_dead_raised) and not knows(party, {t}_u_dead_read) "You know these marks from the old scripts. Round the chalk ring they say what they are for, and they are copied badly: the warding line, the one that keeps the dead off whoever calls them, is not there." teaches {t}_u_dead_read.
  Action {t}_u_raiser_read(actor: group, site: place) "Tell the man with the black candle what his book left out of the ring" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_ossuary) and at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) and able({t}_u_raiser) and knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_read) and state({t}_u_candle, alight).
    Time 0.
    On success { Assert state({t}_u_candle, snuffed). Retract state({t}_u_candle, alight). Retract at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser). }
    Result "You tell him about the warding line. He looks down at the chalk, and you watch him find the place where it should be. His hand shakes when he pinches the candle out. He goes up the stair without looking at the dead, and out of {town} before morning. The book he leaves on the bones.".
  }
  // His while he stands, and only bones once the candle is out: with him gone and it still burning they are no one's,
  // and turn on the living, warning first, so there is a moment to pinch it out.
  Rule {t}_u_dead_masterless when not at({t}_u_raiser, {t}_u_ossuary) and state({t}_u_candle, alight) and tolerates({t}_u_dead, party) says "With no one to hold them, the dead turn their heads toward the living." { Retract tolerates({t}_u_dead, party). }
  Rule {t}_u_dead_masterless_fallen when not able({t}_u_raiser) and state({t}_u_candle, alight) and tolerates({t}_u_dead, party) says "With no one to hold them, the dead turn their heads toward the living." { Retract tolerates({t}_u_dead, party). }
  Rule {t}_u_dead_lie when state({t}_u_candle, snuffed) and at({t}_u_dead, {t}_u_ossuary) and able({t}_u_dead) says "With the candle out, the dead fold down into the bone-heaps like coats let fall, and are only bones again." { Retract at({t}_u_dead, {t}_u_ossuary). Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job). }
  Rule {t}_u_dead_cleared when not able({t}_u_dead) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job). }
  Rule {t}_u_raiser_ended when not able({t}_u_raiser) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser). }
  Objective {t}_u_dead_job_sought when knows(party, {t}_u_notice) and not {t}_u_given({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) toward {t}_priest "Ask {{t}_priest} about what has come up under the churchyard at {town}: the crypt is locked.".
  // Toward the dead themselves and whoever raised them (its own words: "and find out who raised them"), by the
  // churchyard: the crypt is where the priest said they came up, but they are in the
  // ossuary beyond it, and an aim that pointed at the crypt left a company that had been through the ossuary standing
  // in the crypt led only to search it (the owner's play of 11 November: led to the threshold and abandoned there).
  Objective {t}_u_dead_job_aim when {t}_u_given({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) toward {t}_u_dead, {t}_u_raiser by {t}_u_yard "Lay the dead in {{t}_u_crypt} under {{t}_u_yard} at {town}, and find out who raised them.".
  Topic {t}_u_dead_job_paid with {t}_priest "Tell {{t}_priest} the dead under the churchyard are laid, and who raised them" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) and {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) and not {t}_u_halved({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_priest} hears it all with eyes shut, and at the end says the names of the three in the opened graves, one after another. Then 15 coin, and from the shrine's own chest a charm of ashwood and bronze wire, and two small stoppered bottles. 'The charm was made for those who go among the dead,' {{t}_priest} says. 'The bottles are for after.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 15. Give ashwood_charm to actor. Give 2 minor_healing_potion to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_dead_job_rest with {t}_priest "Tell {{t}_priest} who raised the dead under the churchyard" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) and {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) and {t}_u_halved({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_priest} hears it all with eyes shut, and at the end says the names of the three in the opened graves, one after another. Then the rest of the coin, and from the shrine's own chest a charm of ashwood and bronze wire, and two small stoppered bottles. 'The charm was made for those who go among the dead,' {{t}_priest} says. 'The bottles are for after.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Give ashwood_charm to actor. Give 2 minor_healing_potion to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_dead_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_dead_job_half with {t}_priest "Tell {{t}_priest} the dead under the churchyard are laid" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job) once {
    Says "'Laid,' says {{t}_priest}, 'until whoever raised them comes back with another candle.' Ten coin. 'Find who it is, and the rest is yours, and more.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 10. Assert {t}_u_halved({t}_u_dead_job). }
  }
  Objective {t}_u_dead_job_owed when {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) and {t}_u_done({t}_u_raiser) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_dead_job) toward {t}_priest "Tell {{t}_priest} the dead are laid and who raised them, at {{priestat}}: fifteen coin, and what the shrine can give.".
>> 'Whoever will go down into the catacombs under the churchyard, where something has come up: fifteen coin, and the shrine's thanks. Ask {{t}_priest}.'
  Rule {t}_u_dead_onward when {t}_u_done({t}_u_dead_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward). }
--- pit spiders
  // The spiders: the quarry's gate is the inn's, given with the job; the Hobb boy who went in after his ferret saw the
  // mother at the back and dropped his father's knife; the spiders dead and their egg-sacs burned, the inn pays in what
  // a company going on needs, and the knife given back is the Hobbs' to repay.
  Observe {t}_u_pit_scene at {t}_u_pit as fixture when true "A bowl of grey stone cut out of the hill long ago, ivy over its faces; at the bottom, a square adit goes back into the rock behind a barred gate, and a board on the gate says KEEP OUT in three hands.".
  Person {t}_u_spiders "the spiders in the old workings" at {t}_u_gallery {
    Role "cave spiders the size of dogs, that have strung the old workings with web". Species cave_spider. Numbers {brood}. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_gallery.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_spiders) to 60.
  Person {t}_u_mother "the spiders' mother" at {t}_u_brood {
    Role "a spider the size of a pony, swollen and slow, crouched over the eggs at the back of the web". Species cave_spider. Variant brood_mother. Numbers 1. Level 2. Temperament defensive. Lair {t}_u_brood.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_mother) to 120.
  Person {t}_u_hobb "Dannel Hobb" at {innkeeperat} { Role "a boy of ten with a white streak in his hair, kept indoors". Ancestry human. Peaceable. Pronouns he. }
  Entity {t}_u_spiders_job: fact "Burn the spiders out of the quarry adit under the old quarry pit at {town}.".
  Entity {t}_u_spiders_eggs: fact "At the back of the old workings the spiders' mother has hung her eggs: the spiders will come again unless they are burned.".
  Kind hobb_knife "a bone-handled knife" like dagger worth 2 weighing 1 described "A working man's knife with a bone handle, H burned into it.".
  // With the key, a remedy for the bite: a cave spider's venom stays in the blood after the fight, and a lone first
  // company bitten once had died of it at full health (the builder's descent of 8 November).
  Topic {t}_u_spiders_job_ask with {t}_innkeeper "Ask {{t}_innkeeper} about the old quarry" when not {t}_u_given({t}_u_spiders_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) once {
    Says "'Nobody goes in the old quarry now,' says {{t}_innkeeper}. 'There's webs across the adit thick as sailcloth, and the Hobb boy went in after a ferret and came out white. We put a gate on it.' A small key, put down on the counter. 'Twelve coin from the house to whoever burns them out, and a pot of the salve the firemen use. Talk to the boy first. He saw more than he says.' A stoppered phial follows it, the cork waxed. 'Hobb's mother made that, for the bite. Drink it the moment one has you, not after.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_spiders_job). Assert {t}_u_given({t}_u_spiders_job). Give quarry_key to actor. Give antidote to actor. Assert keyholder(actor, {t}_u_adit_lock). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_hobb_told with {t}_u_hobb "Ask Dannel Hobb what he saw in the old quarry" when knows(actor, {t}_u_spiders_job) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_spiders_eggs) once {
    Says "The boy looks at the door before he answers. 'There's a big one at the back,' he says. 'Bigger than a dog. And bags. Hanging up, white, like puddings. They was moving.' He swallows. 'I dropped Dad's knife. Don't tell him.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_spiders_eggs). }
  }
  // A ranger's way (Mission 19): one who reads wild country reads the web at the adit, and knows what the boy saw
  // without asking him.
  Observe {t}_u_adit_web at {t}_u_adit as sign when capable(party, woodcraft) and not knows(party, {t}_u_spiders_eggs) "The web across the cutting is new at the edges and old in the middle, and the drag-lines all run back one way: something big at the back is laying, and has been for a while." teaches {t}_u_spiders_eggs.
  Discovery {t}_u_knife_found "Under the web at the gallery's mouth, a bone-handled knife with an H burned into the handle." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_gallery "Something under the web at the gallery's mouth catches the light.".
  }
  Item {t}_u_knife "a bone-handled knife" is hobb_knife at {t}_u_gallery hidden until {t}_u_knife_found.
  Thing {t}_u_eggs "the spiders' egg-sacs" at {t}_u_brood {
    State hanging "White sacs the size of loaves hang from the roof in a cluster, and something in them moves.".
    State burnt "Where the egg-sacs hung there is a black stain on the roof and a smell of burnt hair.".
    Change burn "Burn the egg-sacs" from hanging to burnt needing flame when not able({t}_u_mother) "The spiders' mother crouches over them, and will not let you near.".
  }
  // An oil firebomb thrown through the crack does for the mother and the eggs both, for a company that would not go in.
  // A flask thrown, or a spell said, takes moments, not a turn of the clock: taking a turn, it had been cut short by the
  // spiders' patience, and a cold player threw it into a fight that said nothing of it (Mission 20, log E32).
  Action {t}_u_brood_burned(actor: group, site: place) "Throw an oil firebomb through the crack into the brood-chamber" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_gallery) and holding(actor, oil_firebomb) and able({t}_u_mother).
    Time 1 minutes.
    On success { Spend oil_firebomb from actor. Slay {t}_u_mother. Retract state({t}_u_eggs, hanging). Assert state({t}_u_eggs, burnt). }
    Result "The flask bursts somewhere behind the web, and the crack fills with light. Something heavy thrashes in there a long while, and then the only sound is the sacs popping in the heat.".
  }
  // A magician's way (Mission 19's Priority Three: a magician's spells should make actual alternatives): fire from the
  // hands, thrown through the crack as the flask is, for no flask.
  Action {t}_u_brood_spelled(actor: group, site: place) "Burn the brood-chamber through the crack with a magician's fire" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_gallery) and able({t}_u_mother) and memberOf(?m, actor) and awake(?m) and (hasCalling(?m, calling_mage) or learned(?m, firebolt) or learned(?m, burning_hands) or learned(?m, scald)).
    Time 1 minutes.
    On success { Slay {t}_u_mother. Retract state({t}_u_eggs, hanging). Assert state({t}_u_eggs, burnt). }
    Result "The words come out cold and the fire comes out hot: it goes through the crack in a sheet, and the web catches like paper. Something heavy thrashes behind it a long while, and then the only sound is the sacs popping in the heat.".
  }
  // A way through for a company that would not stand in the web: an oil firebomb thrown into it from the adit, and the
  // fire runs up it into the gallery. The egg-sacs at the back are still to be seen to.
  Action {t}_u_spiders_burned(actor: group, site: place) "Throw an oil firebomb into the web across the cutting" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_adit) and holding(actor, oil_firebomb) and able({t}_u_spiders).
    Time 1 minutes.
    On success { Spend oil_firebomb from actor. Slay {t}_u_spiders. }
    Result "The flask bursts against the web and the fire runs up it into the dark of the cutting, faster than you would have thought. Something screams in a voice like wet wood in a grate. When it has burned out, nothing moves in there.".
  }
  Rule {t}_u_spiders_cleared when not able({t}_u_spiders) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job). }
  Objective {t}_u_spiders_job_sought when knows(party, {t}_u_notice) and not {t}_u_given({t}_u_spiders_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) toward {t}_innkeeper "Ask {{t}_innkeeper} about the old quarry at {town}: its gate is locked.".
  // Toward where the spiders are, the gallery past the adit: toward the adit, the gold had led back out of the
  // gallery with the spiders in it, "the way you came" (rounds 10 and 11, R and U).
  Objective {t}_u_spiders_job_aim when {t}_u_given({t}_u_spiders_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) toward {t}_u_gallery by {t}_u_pit "Burn the spiders out of {{t}_u_adit} under {{t}_u_pit} at {town}.".
  Objective {t}_u_spiders_job_eggs when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and knows(party, {t}_u_spiders_eggs) and state({t}_u_eggs, hanging) and able({t}_u_mother) toward {t}_u_brood "Deal with the spiders' mother in {{t}_u_brood} behind the quarry's gallery, and burn her eggs, or the spiders will come again.".
  // With her dead, what is left is the eggs: "deal with the spiders' mother" had stood under the fight that killed her
  // (round 10, R 100).
  Objective {t}_u_spiders_job_burn when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and knows(party, {t}_u_spiders_eggs) and state({t}_u_eggs, hanging) and not able({t}_u_mother) toward {t}_u_brood "Burn the spiders' eggs in {{t}_u_brood} behind the quarry's gallery, or the spiders will come again.".
  Topic {t}_u_spiders_job_paid with {t}_innkeeper "Tell {{t}_innkeeper} the spiders in the old quarry are dead, and their eggs burned" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and state({t}_u_eggs, burnt) and not {t}_u_halved({t}_u_spiders_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_innkeeper} counts out 12 coin, and sets a clay pot and a coil of good rope beside it. 'Fireman's salve, and the rope from the gate, which we'll not want now,' {{t}_innkeeper} says.".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 12. Give fireproof_salve to actor. Give rope to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_spiders_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_spiders_job_rest with {t}_innkeeper "Tell {{t}_innkeeper} the spiders' eggs in the old quarry are burned" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and state({t}_u_eggs, burnt) and {t}_u_halved({t}_u_spiders_job) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job) once {
    Says "{{t}_innkeeper} counts out the other five coin, and sets a clay pot and a coil of good rope beside it. 'Fireman's salve, and the rope from the gate, which we'll not want now,' {{t}_innkeeper} says.".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Give fireproof_salve to actor. Give rope to actor. Assert {t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job). Retract knows(actor, {t}_u_spiders_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_spiders_job_half with {t}_innkeeper "Tell {{t}_innkeeper} the spiders in the old quarry are dead" when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and state({t}_u_eggs, hanging) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job) once {
    Says "'And the eggs?' says {{t}_innkeeper}, and sees your face. 'Then they'll be back by spring.' Seven coin. 'Burn them and the rest is yours.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 7. Assert {t}_u_halved({t}_u_spiders_job). }
  }
  Topic {t}_u_hobb_knife with {t}_u_hobb "Give Dannel Hobb his father's knife back" when holding(actor, hobb_knife) once {
    Says "The boy takes it in both hands. That evening his mother comes to find you, with a bottle wrapped in a cloth. 'From the boy,' she says. 'It's what I had by me.'".
    On discuss { Spend hobb_knife from actor. Give minor_healing_potion to actor. }
  }
  Objective {t}_u_spiders_job_owed when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and state({t}_u_eggs, burnt) and not {t}_u_paid({t}_u_spiders_job) toward {t}_innkeeper "Tell {{t}_innkeeper} the spiders are dead and their eggs burned, at {{innkeeperat}}: twelve coin, salve and rope.".
>> 'SPIDERS in the old quarry. Twelve coin from the house. Ask {{t}_innkeeper} for the gate key.'
  Rule {t}_u_spiders_onward when {t}_u_done({t}_u_spiders_job) and not {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward) { Assert {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward). }
--- below
  Place {t}_u_drain "the old drain" is room within {t} at 0, 5 underground 2 down.
  Passage {t}_u_drain_way "a culvert going down" is crawl between {t}_u_warren and {t}_u_drain.
  // A job done under the town is not the end of what is under it (the owner, 8 November: a dungeon is more than one or
  // two rooms; the undertown's three ways meet, and go on down, and nothing had said so). Each trouble, done, says the
  // old ways go on; the undercroft they meet in is the next place to go, its floor the next thing to try, its vault's
  // keeper the next to face; and below him the deep site (see RegionUndertown).
  Entity {t}_u_onward: fact "".
  Objective {t}_u_onward_sought when {t}_u_done({t}_u_onward) and not been(party, {t}_u_undercroft) "The old ways under {town} go on past the corn-store's cellar: the rat-runs into an old drain, the ossuary down steps behind the bone-heaps, the quarry gallery through a breach in its floor. They meet below, in {{t}_u_undercroft}.".
  Objective {t}_u_floor_sought when been(party, {t}_u_undercroft) and not knows(party, {t}_u_vault_found) toward {t}_u_undercroft "Something is under the floor of {{t}_u_undercroft}: one flag cut with letters does not sit level. The same ring may be cut somewhere in the ways down to it.".
  Place {t}_u_undercroft "the undercroft" is room within {t} at 1, 5 underground 2 down.
  Passage {t}_u_drain_mouth "the mouth of the drain" is passage between {t}_u_drain and {t}_u_undercroft.
  // Each way down is more than the room its job ends in (the owner, 8 November: a dungeon is more than one or two
  // rooms): behind the bone-heaps a charnel passage where the raiser's first tries were left to stand, and off the
  // gallery the old working face the spiders came up from, a beetles' nest now.
  Place {t}_u_charnel "the charnel passage" is room within {t} at 1, 4 underground 2 down.
  Passage {t}_u_charnel_arch "a low arch behind the bone-heaps" is passage between {t}_u_ossuary and {t}_u_charnel.
  Passage {t}_u_ossuary_steps "steps down behind the bone-heaps" is steps between {t}_u_charnel and {t}_u_undercroft.
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_charnel).
  Observe {t}_u_charnel_scene at {t}_u_charnel as fixture when true "A long low passage lined with shelves of the older dead, wrapped in cloth gone brown. Some of the shelves are empty, and the cloth on the floor under them is torn.".
  Person {t}_u_shamblers "the dead in the charnel passage" at {t}_u_charnel {
    Role "the raiser's first tries, stood up off the shelves and left where they stood". Species zombie. Numbers {pair}. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_charnel.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_shamblers) to 90.
  Discovery {t}_u_charnel_goods "On the last shelf, under a fall of cloth, what the old dead were buried with: nobody has been down to take it." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_charnel "Under the cloth on the last shelf, something hard and cold.".
  }
  Item {t}_u_charnel_plate "a silver grave-plate" is chapel_plate at {t}_u_charnel hidden until {t}_u_charnel_goods.
  Item {t}_u_charnel_torc "an iron torc" is iron_torc at {t}_u_charnel hidden until {t}_u_charnel_goods.
  Item {t}_u_charnel_bracelet "a bronze bracelet" is bronze_bracelet at {t}_u_charnel hidden until {t}_u_charnel_goods.
  Place {t}_u_face "the old working face" is room within {t} at 2, 5 underground 2 down.
  Passage {t}_u_face_way "a cut going on past the web" is passage between {t}_u_gallery and {t}_u_face.
  Passage {t}_u_gallery_breach "a breach in the gallery floor" is crawl between {t}_u_face and {t}_u_undercroft.
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_face).
  Observe {t}_u_face_scene at {t}_u_face as fixture when true "Where the quarrymen stopped: a face of stone with the pick-marks still on it, a rotten ladder, and the floor broken through in one corner into somewhere older underneath. Things click and scuttle in the spoil.".
  Person {t}_u_beetles "the beetles in the spoil" at {t}_u_face {
    Role "beetles as long as a forearm, nesting in the quarrymen's spoil". Species beetle. Numbers {pack}. Level 1. Temperament defensive. Lair {t}_u_face.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_beetles) to 60.
  Discovery {t}_u_face_tools "Under the ladder, a quarryman's bag, left when the face was given up: his tools, and his wages, never collected." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_face "A leather bag under the ladder, stiff with age.".
  }
  Item {t}_u_face_crowbar "a quarryman's crowbar" is crowbar at {t}_u_face hidden until {t}_u_face_tools.
  Item {t}_u_face_purse "a quarryman's wages" is steel_coin at {t}_u_face hidden until {t}_u_face_tools.
  Item {t}_u_face_garnet "a garnet in the spoil" is garnet at {t}_u_face hidden until {t}_u_face_tools.
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_drain). Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_undercroft).
  // Where the three ways meet, nothing lives: a company can rest there between them (the builder's descent of 8
  // November: nowhere under the town could a company recover, and a lone warrior went into her seventh fight hurt).
  Initially Assert restful({t}_u_undercroft).
  Observe {t}_u_drain_scene at {t}_u_drain as fixture when true "An old drain of fitted stone, tall enough to stoop along, with a black trickle down the middle of it and the walls furred with something pale that moves when the light touches it.".
  Observe {t}_u_undercroft_scene at {t}_u_undercroft as fixture when true "A long room of round pillars, older than anything above it: the corn-store, the church and the quarry were all dug down into it, from three sides, by people who did not know it was here.".
  // The flag is a sign of its own, so the page says it apart and searching is the act it leads with.
  Observe {t}_u_undercroft_flag at {t}_u_undercroft as sign when not knows(party, {t}_u_vault_found) "One flag in the middle of the floor is cut with a ring of letters nobody here can read, and it does not sit quite level with the rest.".
  Person {t}_u_crawler "a great centipede" at {t}_u_drain {
    Role "a centipede as long as a man, living in the old drain". Species great_centipede. Numbers 1. Level 2. Lair {t}_u_drain.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_crawler) to 60.
  Discovery {t}_u_drain_cache_found "Wedged in the drain where the water would have carried it, a purse someone dropped down a grating long ago." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_drain "Something wedged in the drain, where the water left it.".
  }
  Item {t}_u_drain_purse "a mouldy purse" is steel_coin at {t}_u_drain hidden until {t}_u_drain_cache_found.
--- vault
  // The lettered flag is a lock with no keyhole (the owner, 8 November: a dungeon has at least one puzzle). Its ring of
  // letters is the makers' own, and the same ring is cut, smaller, in each of the three ways down to it, over the
  // oldest thing there: read in any of them, the letters to press are the three cut deeper than the rest. One who
  // knows old writing reads them off the flag itself. A strong arm can lever it up instead, slowly, and loudly.
  Entity {t}_u_vault_found: fact "The lettered flag in the undercroft floor lifts: under it, a stair going down into the dark.".
  // Said as what is seen where it is found: told "on the undercroft's flag … here too", it had spoken of an undercroft
  // the company had never seen (rounds 10 and 11, R 107, U 135).
  Discovery {t}_u_letters "A ring of letters cut small over the oldest stone of the old work, three of them cut deeper than the rest and worn smooth by thumbs, as if they were pressed." {
    Found by searching {t}_u_ossuary "Over the oldest niche, behind the bone-heaps, a ring of letters cut small, three of them deeper than the rest.".
    Found by searching {t}_u_brood "Under the webs, on the one dressed stone in the chamber's wall, a ring of letters cut small, three of them worn deep.".
    Found by searching {t}_u_drain "On the keystone where the drain meets the old work, a ring of letters cut small, three of them worn deep.".
  }
  Action {t}_u_flag_pressed(actor: group, site: place) "Press the three deep-cut letters on the flag, as the ring below has them" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_undercroft) and knows(actor, {t}_u_letters) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_vault_found).
    Time 1.
    On success { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_vault_found). }
    Result "One, and the next, and the last: each gives a little under your thumb, with a click somewhere under the floor. The flag sinks a finger's width, and slides aside on its own weight. Under it, a stair goes down into the dark.".
  }
  Action {t}_u_flag_read(actor: group, site: place) "Read the ring of letters on the flag" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_undercroft) and capable(actor, lore) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_letters) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_vault_found).
    Time 1.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_letters). }
    Result "The letters are the makers' own, and run round the flag twice over in a pattern that is not a word at all but a count: three of them, read as numbers, are cut deeper than the rest. Pressed in their order, they would be the key.".
    Otherwise "The letters are the makers' own, and you cannot make them out. The same ring may be cut somewhere else, where whoever cut it meant it to be read.".
  }
  Action {t}_u_flag_levered(actor: group, site: place) "Lever the lettered flag up by main force" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, {t}_u_undercroft) and not knows(actor, {t}_u_vault_found).
    Time 6.
    Resolve check(actor, brawn, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, {t}_u_vault_found). }
    Result "It takes most of an hour, and the edge of everything you have that will take a strain. The flag comes up grinding, and something in the floor below breaks with a sound like a bell. Under it, a stair goes down into the dark, and below, something has heard you.".
    Otherwise "The flag does not move, and an hour is gone. It was not made to be lifted.".
  }
  Place {t}_u_vault "the sealed vault" is room within {t} at 1, 6 underground 3 down.
  Passage {t}_u_vault_stair "the stair under the lettered flag" is stair between {t}_u_undercroft and {t}_u_vault hidden until {t}_u_vault_found.
  Initially Assert unlit({t}_u_vault).
  Observe {t}_u_vault_scene at {t}_u_vault as fixture when true "A small square vault, dry as an oven, with a stone chair at the far end and niches in the walls where something was kept, and a smell of old spice.".
  Person {t}_u_keeper "the keeper of the vault" at {t}_u_vault {
    Role "the last of whoever built the undercroft, long dead and still at its post". Species ghoul. Numbers 1. Level 2. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_u_vault.
    Warns "Something stands up from a stone chair at the far end of the vault, slowly, as if it had been waiting a long time.".
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_u_keeper) to 300.
  Item {t}_u_vault_rings "a cord of old rings" is grave_rings at {t}_u_vault.
  Item {t}_u_vault_stone "a moonstone the size of a thumb" is moonstone at {t}_u_vault.
  Milestone {t}_u_vault_reached "found the sealed vault under the undercroft" worth 25 when been(party, {t}_u_vault).
  Objective {t}_u_vault_sought when knows(party, {t}_u_vault_found) and able({t}_u_keeper) toward {t}_u_vault "Something keeps {{t}_u_vault} under the undercroft.".
